age->matte is set true by the extra_samples detection but then... Actually the description says opacity channel NOT assured to be initialized in RGBAStrippedMethod case. Where? If `image->matte` false, opacity not set. But then resize uses `source->matte || colorspace==CMYK` to decide whether to read opacity. So if image->matte false, it won't read opacity. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the issue: image->matte is true but the strip data doesn't actually have alpha? TIFFGetA reads from 32-bit value that libtiff fills; if no alpha, TIFFGetA returns 0xFF presumably. That's initialized.\n\nHold on. Let me look at actual uninit: MSAN says uninitialized created in SetCacheViewPixels at tiff.c:2994. That's line 2994 which is inside RGBAStrippedMethod? Let me check exact line.\n\nLine 2994: let me view around.\n\nFrom earlier: case RGBAStrippedMethod starts at 2940. Around 2994 is `p=strip_pixels+image->columns*i;`? Let me check.\n\nActually the trace: `SetCacheViewPixels` called from `ReadTIFFImage tiff.c:2994`. Let me get exact line 2994."}}
